The Tokenizers module of ObjCTokenizer (ObjCTokenizer/OCT*.{h,m}) is a
port to Objective-C of the Sources/Tokenizers Swift module from
swift-transformers release tag 1.3.2 (May 6, 2026). The Swift original is © HuggingFace, Inc.
and is distributed under the Apache 2.0 license. A copy of the Apache 2.0
license is reproduced below.

Per Apache 2.0 §4(b), modifications were made: the Swift sources were
translated to Objective-C using only Foundation primitives. The Hub,
Generation, and Models modules from swift-transformers were not ported.

The port also incorporates the following Tokenizers fixes made upstream
after tag 1.3.2, up to swift-transformers commit 2590d23 (October 13, 2026):

  #388  Unigram: honor byte_fallback on encode
  #389  Reuse byte fallback table in BPE and Unigram
  #390  Honor byte_fallback configuration value in BPE
  #395  Match Rust tokenizers on code points in Replace, Metaspace and
        BPE merges
  #397  Honor ignore_merges in BPE
  #400  Respect addSpecialTokens in RobertaProcessing
  #407  Throw on invalid regex rather than silently ignoring

Where a fix still differed from the Rust reference, the Rust code was ported
instead (BPE byte fallback and unknown-token handling follow `merge_word`).

Parts of ObjCTokenizer are ports to Objective-C of HuggingFace's Rust
`tokenizers` library (https://github.com/huggingface/tokenizers) and of the
`spm_precompiled` crate (https://github.com/huggingface/spm_precompiled),
both © HuggingFace, Inc. and licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:
the BPE `merge_word` symbol setup (OCTBPE.m), Unigram byte fallback
(OCTUnigram.m), the Metaspace decoder (OCTDecoder.m), and the Precompiled
normalizer with its double-array trie (OCTNormalizer.m).

